[{"id":"carry-predict-carry","itemId":"carry-chain","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">add8</code> adds two 8-bit numbers, <code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code>, into a 9-bit <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code>. Its top bit, <code class=\"nobreak\">sum[8]</code>, is the carry out of bit 7: 1 when <code>a + b</code> is more than FF. <code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code> are drawn in hexadecimal, a new pair every 10 ns step. Steps 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">sum[8]</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>FF + 01 and F0 + 10 both make 100, nine bits, so <code class=\"nobreak\">sum[8]</code> is 1 in steps 2 and 4, as it was for 80 + 80 in step 1. 7F + 01 is 80 and 80 + 7F is FF: both still fit in eight bits, so <code class=\"nobreak\">sum[8]</code> is 0. The carry chain works out every bit's carry, and the last carry is <code class=\"nobreak\">sum[8]</code>.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"add8-carry","source":"hdl/level-06/add8/add8_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":6,"signals":[{"label":"a[7:0]","path":"add8_tb.a","width":8,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00000001"],[1,"10000000"],[2,"11111111"],[3,"01111111"],[4,"11110000"],[5,"10000000"]]},{"label":"b[7:0]","path":"add8_tb.b","width":8,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00000010"],[1,"10000000"],[2,"00000001"],[4,"00010000"],[5,"01111111"]]},{"label":"sum[8]","path":"add8_tb.carry","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"]],"samples":["0","1","1","0","1","0"]}]},"answer":"sum[8]","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"carry-report-blink","itemId":"carry-chain","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built level 2's <code class=\"nobreak\">blink</code> for the Arty A7-100T. Its 27-bit <code class=\"nobreak\">count</code> adds 1 at every rising edge while <code class=\"nobreak\">run</code> is 1, and the LED shows its top bit. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the CARRY4 row. A CARRY4 is four bits of carry chain, so 27 bits need seven of them, the last one using three bits: six would cover only 24, and one for each bit would be 27. The FDRE row is <code class=\"nobreak\">count</code> itself, and the single LUT shows how little else adding 1 needs: the carry chain does the counting.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/blink/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":180,"excerpt":["+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| FDRE     |   27 |        Flop & Latch |","| CARRY4   |    7 |          CarryLogic |","| IBUF     |    3 |                  IO |","| OBUF     |    1 |                  IO |","| LUT1     |    1 |                 LUT |","| BUFG     |    1 |               Clock |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many CARRY4 cells does blink use?","answer":"7","numeric":true},{"id":"carry-fill-width","itemId":"carry-chain","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">add8</code> adds two 8-bit numbers, <code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code>, and must keep the carry out of bit 7, so that FF + FF gives 1FE. Fill in the range of <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code>.","explanationHtml":"<p>The largest sum, FF + FF = 1FE, needs nine bits, one more than either input, so <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code> is <code class=\"nobreak\">[8:0]</code>. With <code class=\"nobreak\">[7:0]</code> the carry out would be lost, as lesson 1.1's lost bit was: the carry chain still works it out, but nothing keeps it.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-06/add8/add8.sv","firstLine":3,"totalLines":9,"before":["module add8 (","  input  logic [7:0] a,","  input  logic [7:0] b,"],"blankLine":{"left":"  output logic ","right":" sum"},"after":[");","  assign sum = a + b;","endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"add8","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"7","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] a,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"7","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] b,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":" sum","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" sum ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" a ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"+","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" b;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["[8:0]"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The range of sum"},{"id":"carry-report-add8","itemId":"carry-chain","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built <code class=\"nobreak\">add8</code>, which adds two 8-bit numbers from pins, <code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code>, and drives <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code> to pins. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the LUT2 row: one for each bit. Each bit of the sum combines a bit of <code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> and a bit of <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code>, and that takes a LUT before the carry chain can use it. A counter adds a constant 1, so it needs almost none (level 2's <code class=\"nobreak\">blink</code> has a single LUT for 27 bits).</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/add8/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":180,"excerpt":["+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |   16 |                  IO |","| OBUF     |    9 |                  IO |","| LUT2     |    8 |                 LUT |","| CARRY4   |    3 |          CarryLogic |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many LUT2 cells does add8 use?","answer":"8","numeric":true}]